op a segment?", "Contribution 300,000; avoidable fixed costs 340,000", "________"], ["Add a segment?", "Contribution 500,000; new fixed costs 380,000; cannibalises 90,000", "________"], ["Second shift?", "Adds 700,000 of fixed cost; contribution 3.50 a unit", "________"], ["After-tax value of a 120,000 gain", "Tax rate 25 per cent", "________"], ["Break-even cannibalisation on the added segment", "", "________"]], [["English (exam term)", "العربية", "Français"], ["break-even cannibalisation", "حد التآكل المتعادل", "seuil de cannibalisation"], ["widen the boundary", "توسيع نطاق التحليل", "élargir le périmètre"], ["defend an estimate", "الدفاع عن التقدير", "justifier une estimation"], ["course of action", "مسار العمل", "ligne de conduite"]], [["Decision", "Answer"], ["Process further?", "Yes: the incremental revenue is 62.00 − 40.00 = 22.00 against a cost of 18.00, a gain of 4.00 a unit."], ["Drop a segment?", "Drop it: avoidable fixed costs of 340,000 exceed the contribution of 300,000 by 40,000."], ["Add a segment?", "Add it: 500,000 − 380,000 = 120,000 of gain, less 90,000 of cannibalisation, leaves 30,000."], ["Second shift?", "It needs 200,000 extra units: 700,000 ÷ 3.50 = 200,000."], ["After-tax value of a 120,000 gain", "90,000: 120,000 × 0.75 = 90,000."], ["Break-even cannibalisation", "120,000 of contribution: the gain before cannibalisation is 120,000, so anything above that reverses the decision."], ["What it tells you", "Three of the four decisions are close: 4.00 a unit, 40,000 a year and 30,000 a year are all small enough that an error in one estimate would reverse them. Only the shift question has a clear answer, and it is a question about demand rather than about cost."]]], "figures": {"F709-01": 0, "F709-02": 2, "F709-03": 4, "F709-04": 6, "F709-05": 8, "F709-06": 10, "F709-07": 12}, "tsec": {"0": "", "1": "", "2": "9.1", "3": "9.1", "4": "9.2", "5": "9.2", "6": "9.3", "7": "9.3", "8": "9.4", "9": "9.4", "10": "9.5", "11": "9.5", "12": "9.5"}}